{
  "dom_id": "step-q53668",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given that $△ABC∼△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ $AB=4\\,cm$ and $BC=6\\,cm,$\nwhich of the following could be the values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}?$\n\nI. ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}=16\\,cm,\\,{B}^{′}{C}^{′}=24\\,cm$\n\nII. ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}=20\\,cm,\\,{B}^{′}{C}^{′}=30\\,cm$\n\nIII. ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}=32\\,cm,\\,{B}^{′}{C}^{′}=42\\,cm$",
  "worked_solution": "For similar polygons, the ratios of lengths of the corresponding sides should be the same.\n\n- Let's check for this in option I:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{AB}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}} & =\\frac{4}{16}=\\frac{1}{4}, \\\\ \\frac{BC}{{B}^{′}{C}^{′}} & =\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option I does give possible values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}.$\n\n- For option II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{AB}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}} & =\\frac{4}{20}=\\frac{1}{5}, \\\\ \\frac{BC}{{B}^{′}{C}^{′}} & =\\frac{6}{30}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option II does give possible values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}.$\n\n- For option III, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{AB}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}} & =\\frac{4}{32}=\\frac{1}{8}, \\\\ \\frac{BC}{{B}^{′}{C}^{′}} & =\\frac{6}{42}=\\frac{1}{7}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, option III does not give possible values of ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}{C}^{′}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "selection",
      "type": "radio",
      "choices": [
        {
          "option": "a",
